  "query_preview": "..High pressure centered over southern Utah this\nevening will remain in place through Sunday while heights continue\nto rise. Patchy high clouds this evening will clear out late\ntonight resulting in fewer clouds on Sunday. Temperatures are\nexpected to continue trending slightly upward for Sunday.\n\nOn Monday, a weakening trough is still progged to make its way\ninto the Great Basin, crossing Utah Monday night through Tuesday.\nThis trough will bring a slight decrease in moisture and spotty \nlight precipitation. The NBM has a 15-25% chance of the mountains \nseeing 0.05 inches of precipitation or greater, with generally a\n5% chance or less in the valleys. \n\nHigh pressure is expected to rebound for late week ahead of a\npotentially stronger trough for the weekend or early next week.\nCluster analysis of global ensembles favor some flavor of trough\nduring this timeframe, but there is still some spread with regards\nto timing and strength. A stronger/slower solution currently \nlooks more favorable, encompassing around 55% of members.",
